    {
      "id": "claim_8fd073255e854b869bc4ae533bea9ac9",
      "statement": "The JS engine is rusty_v8 directly, one isolate per cell: a worker's default-export fetch receives an env whose bindings are Durable Object namespaces, and DO storage is async in JS but synchronous underneath (sync Rust ops wrapped in async by the JS harness).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/js.rs#L8-L15",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a3d6723fd7461ff73e7bdc96a3de3ba2066f8cf9005123a51731700b09dd97a2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b06d640824124dc099ac32edc66c94de",
      "statement": "The isolate pool is the shell around the pure isolate decision core: one multi-threaded Tokio runtime owns every socket and timer, isolates belong to no thread because v8::Locker installs the entering thread's per-isolate state, and every choice about which isolate to grow, shed, or retire is made by celld_logic::isolate and merely performed here.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/pool.rs#L7-L20",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7902e474f5bb600a444576d13baf3cb51c8e12a1ef08348a4c6a9587245af534:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_13521534d32b4c299bd761f50b55bbdb",
      "statement": "The isolate core tracks three quantities per isolate: turns (CPU demand, released across an await), requests (affiliation into the isolate's heap), and cells (realms the isolate is committed to); max_requests is a node-wide bound while max_cells is per-isolate, because a heap holding too many cells is a single OOM taking every cell down together.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/isolate.rs#L3-L88",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e57bec10c3031ec08d5f82cce124b28dad14402a00a562adaa1093041919aa60:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3fdbd237149c47cd81143d32d6620c59",
      "statement": "The prelude and harness compile once per process and are cached so a new isolate pays for execution but not compilation, while the per-worker bindings (env, routing table, compatibility flags) are built every time; this matters because every cell wake pays a fresh isolate.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/js/bootstrap.rs#L1-L16",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b3df8c6c63b3f8e98f44bab5683e0abe5f577b686020fca8b49b7d9e1b4a00d9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5eadb858fc0549b098d2af954ed51fb7",
      "statement": "Module resolution distinguishes builtins whose source the runtime holds from imports of another worker that resolve through the loader, and most builtins are lazy so a worker that never touches a module never compiles it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/js/modules.rs#L1-L25",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c5fb98a21634bbab5d664a60bc4dc77f142b0096af7a1751b19421c15bd167d3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_963e8cf649d14ce6bc1db63d079b45e3",
      "statement": "Cell storage is per-cell SQLite in WAL mode backing ctx.storage: each cell is its own database file and bucket prefix, the JS thread holds a scope-to-connection map (open on activate, close on evict), and a dedicated alarm table records committed alarm mutations that no turn has taken yet.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/storage.rs#L1-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ffc1f9ef3a7e99a6fb640ea7c9906b014271d778590eb094ad78b10005536bd4:"
